Package: winiso-ng
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: SysArchX <354081608+SysArchX@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/SysArchX/WinIso-NG
Depends: python3 (>= 3.6),
         python3-wxgtk4.0,
         python3-termcolor,
         p7zip-full,
         parted,
         dosfstools,
         ntfs-3g,
         e2fsprogs,
         util-linux,
         coreutils,
         grub2-common | grub-common
Recommends: exfatprogs,
            udftools,
            pkexec | policykit-1
Suggests: mtools
Description: create bootable Windows and Linux USB installers (Rufus-style GUI)
 WinIso-NG writes ISO or IMG images to a USB storage device, creating a
 bootable Windows installer (or any other bootable image) from the Linux
 desktop. It is a fork of WoeUSB-ng with a Rufus-inspired form and a dark
 neon interface.
 .
 Features:
  * Disk or ISO image, DD raw image mode and non-bootable (format only) modes
  * MBR and GPT partition tables
  * FAT32, NTFS, exFAT and UDF target filesystems with selectable cluster size
  * Quick format, destructive bad blocks check and image checksums
    (MD5, SHA-1, SHA-256, SHA-512)
  * Legacy BIOS boot through GRUB, native UEFI boot and UEFI:NTFS support for
    images whose install.wim exceeds the FAT32 4 GiB file size limit
  * Live log window and inline progress reporting
